  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Anik Milk Products Private Limited vs Suresh Kumar Agarwal And Ors on 10 September, 2024 Ocdsl-1 Order SHEET IP-COM/27/2024 IA No. GA-COM/1/2024 IN THE HIGH COURT AT CALCUTTA COMMERCIAL DIVISION ORIGINAL SIDE ANIK MILK PRODUCTS PRIVATE LIMITED Vs SURESH KUMAR AGARWAL AND ORS BEFORE: The Hon'ble JUSTICE KRISHNA RAO Date : September 10, 2024. Appearance: Mr. Soumya Ray Chowdhury, Adv. Ms. Susrea Mitra, Adv. Mr. Amandeep Singh, Adv. Mr. Riyanshu Agarwal, Adv. Ms. Bhawna Tikrewal, Adv. Mr. Soumo Chaudhury, Adv. ... for the plaintiff The Court:",
    "facts": "The plaintiff has prayed for leave under Clause 12 of the Letters Patent on the ground that the plaintiff is outside the jurisdiction of this Court but the defendant nos. 1 and 2 are within the jurisdiction of this Court. Accordingly, the plaintiff has not initiated pre institution mediation process. Accordingly, leave under Section 12A of the Commercial Courts Act is granted. The plaintiff has filed the present application for grant of ad interim order. The trademarks obtained by the Anik Industries Limited is still valid and subsisting. The plaintiff after obtaining the trademark applied to the Trademark Registry for getting its name 4 registered as a subsequent proprietor of the said trademarks. The mark Anik Milk Products Private Limited vs Suresh Kumar Agarwal And Ors on 10 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/169419171/ 3 \"ANIK\" along with a unique get-up, packaging, colour combination was continuously and extensively and uninterruptedly used by the plaintiff through its predecessor-in-title for the last more than five decades. In order to protect its customers from getting deceived and have health issues, the plaintiff employed and authorized dealers in parts of India for distributing and supplying the ghee products. By virtue of extensive, open, continuous and uninterrupted usage of the plaintiff's ghee product bearing the unique and distinct get-up, colour combination and packaging, trade dress under the trademark \"ANIK\" since 1965, the said mark has become inseparably and exclusively associated with the business identity of the plaintiff. The plaintiff's well-known trademark \"ANIK\" has become a prominent name in the dairy business which is used by the plaintiff as a house mark in respect of well-known and widely accepted products. Due to such prominence of the plaintiff's mark \"ANIK\" the ghee products bearing the trade dress has also achieved substantial goodwill, reputation and recognition in the market.",
    "arguments": "Counsel for the plaintiff submits that the trademark \"ANIK\" and trade dress of the plaintiff are inherently a distinctive one and the 6 customers will assume that the spurious inferior quality ghee product bearing the identical and deceptively similar trademark and the trade dress Anik Milk Products Private Limited vs Suresh Kumar Agarwal And Ors on 10 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/169419171/ 5 of the defendant are either an offshoot of the plaintiff's mark or the defendants somehow are associated or connected with the plaintiff or its business. Counsel for the plaintiff submits that the act of infringement has been committed by the defendants as the defendants have purportedly used the plaintiff's trademark \"ANIK\" and trade dress in attempt to imitate authentic trademark/corporate name, domain name of the plaintiff with an intention to escape liabilities, if possible, in such a manner which has caused confusion and/or deception in the mind of public and the members of the trade as regards the source and origin of the goods. Counsel for the plaintiff submits that the defendants have no right to use the trademark \"ANIK\" and the trade dress in any manner whatsoever in respect of their spurious ghee products. He submits that the plaintiff has not permitted nor has granted any licence to the defendants to use the trademark \"ANIK\" and the trade dress or any other identical or deceptively similar mark and thus, the use of the same is clearly unauthorized, mala fide intention of the defendants to make illegal and wrongful gain from the immense goodwill and reputation gained by the plaintiff for the last more than five decades."
  },
